        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Pathfinder v1.0",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "USES_PHYSICAL_SCHEME",
            "target_entity_instance": "Bayesian inference",
            "target_entity_type": "PhysicalScheme",
            "paragraph": "Bayesian inference allows assimilating observational data into reduced-complexity models such as Pathfinder\u2076\u2074. Conceptually, posterior probability distributions of parameters are deduced by merging a priori knowledge on the distributions of these parameters and on distributions of observations of some of the model's simulated variables, using Bayes' law\u2076\u2075.",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": false
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "DICE-2016R2",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "HAS_SUBSEQUENT_VERSION",
            "target_entity_instance": "updated DICE",
            "target_entity_type": "Source",
            "paragraph": "Our version of DICE is the published DICE-2016R2 version\u00b9\u00b2 with the following additional updates\u00b2\u2077: economic damage function\u2078\u00b3, pure rate of time preference and intertemporal elasticity of substitution\u2078\u2074, and constraints on technical feasibility (emissions reduction of no more than 10 GtCO2 per 5-year period, abatement rate increase of at most 10% per 5-year period, and availability of net-negative emissions technology as of 2045).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Pathfinder v1.0",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "APPLIES_TO_REALM",
            "target_entity_instance": "landIce",
            "target_entity_type": "Realm",
            "paragraph": "Sea level rise (SLR) is split into a thermosteric contribution and three ice-related ones: glaciers, Greenland ice sheets, and Antarctica ice sheets.",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": false,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Pathfinder v1.0",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "APPLIES_TO_REALM",
            "target_entity_instance": "ocean",
            "target_entity_type": "Realm",
            "paragraph": "The ocean carbon cycle follows the structure of the Bern Simple Climate Model\u2075\u2078. The land carbon cycle follows the formulation of the compact Earth system model OSCAR\u2075\u2079, although it is aggregated into one global biome, land use change is ignored, and a fraction of soil carbon pool is assumed passive\u2076\u2070. Emissions from permafrost thaw are calculated with the emulator from ref\u00b3\u2077, but aggregated into one unique region. Sea level rise (SLR) is split into a thermosteric contribution and three ice-related ones: glaciers, Greenland ice sheets, and Antarctica ice sheets. The thermosteric effect is a linear function of the oceanic heat content\u00b3\u2070,\u2076\u00b9, and each ice-related effect follows a first-order differential equation\u2076\u00b2 driven by a non-linear function of GSAT change. Additionally, ocean surface acidification follows a polynomial fit on atmospheric CO2 concentration \u2076\u00b3.",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": false,
            "eval": false
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Pathfinder v1.0",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "APPLIES_TO_REALM",
            "target_entity_instance": "land",
            "target_entity_type": "Realm",
            "paragraph": "The land carbon cycle follows the formulation of the compact Earth system model OSCAR\u2075\u2079, although it is aggregated into one global biome, land use change is ignored, and a fraction of soil carbon pool is assumed passive\u2076\u2070. Emissions from permafrost thaw are calculated with the emulator from ref\u00b3\u2077, but aggregated into one unique region.",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": false,
            "eval": false
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Pathfinder v1.0",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "APPLIES_TO_REALM",
            "target_entity_instance": "atmos",
            "target_entity_type": "Realm",
            "paragraph": "The climate subcomponent that links global surface air temperature (GSAT) to effective radiative forcing (ERF) follows a widely used 2-box model with deep ocean heat uptake efficacy\u2075\u2075. We note this is a structure similar to that of the original DICE, albeit with time-dependent climate feedback factor and drastically revised parameters' values. The total ERF is caused by atmospheric CO2 (following the IPCC AR5 logarithmic formula\u2075\u2077) and an aggregate of non-CO2 species (provided as exogenous time series). Atmospheric CO2 is calculated as the balance between industrial CO2 emissions (determined by the economic module), land use CO2 emissions (provided as exogenous time series), ocean and land carbon sinks, and permafrost carbon emissions.",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": false,
            "eval": true
        }
